.TH GALAXY-TERMINAL 1 "September 2026" "Galaxy Terminal 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
galaxy-terminal \- GTK 3 and XApp terminal for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B galaxy-terminal
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ --
.IR COMMAND " " ARG ...]
.br
.B galaxy-terminal
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B -e
.IR COMMAND " " ARG ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Galaxy Terminal uses VTE for terminal emulation and provides tabs, profiles,
searchable scrollback, configurable shortcuts and an XApp preferences window.
It requires a Wayland session. It does not restore closed sessions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --new-tab
Open in the active terminal window, or a new window if none exists.
.TP
.B --new-window
Open a new window. This takes precedence over --new-tab.
.TP
.BI --profile= NAME
Use a configured profile.
.TP
.BI --working-directory= DIR
Start in DIR. Relative paths are resolved against the invoking process's directory.
.TP
.BI --title= TITLE
.TQ
.BI "-T " TITLE
Set a custom tab title. Empty uses the shell-reported title.
.TP
.BI "-e " "COMMAND ARG..."
.TQ
.BI "--execute " "COMMAND ARG..."
.TQ
.BI "-- " "COMMAND ARG..."
Run an executable with arguments. All following arguments belong to that command.
No implicit shell evaluation is performed; invoke sh -c explicitly when needed.
.TP
.B --help
Show help locally without affecting another running instance.
.TP
.B --version
Show the application version locally.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+Shift+T opens a tab; Ctrl+Shift+N opens a window; Ctrl+Shift+W closes a tab.
Ctrl+Shift+C/V copies/pastes. Ctrl+Shift+F searches retained output.
Ctrl+Page Up/Down changes tabs. Alt+1 through Alt+8 selects numbered tabs;
Alt+9 selects the last. Ctrl with the plus/minus character zooms in/out;
Ctrl+0 resets zoom. Ctrl+comma opens preferences. F11 toggles fullscreen.
All bindings can be changed or disabled in preferences.
.PP
In search, Enter/Shift+Enter finds the next/previous match; Escape closes search.
Ctrl+Left/Right remain available for shell word navigation by default.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/galaxy-terminal/settings.ini
or
.I ~/.config/galaxy-terminal/settings.ini
stores general settings, profiles and shortcuts. GUI changes are debounced and
saved automatically. External edits reload; valid external edits take precedence
over pending GUI changes. Syntax errors retain usable in-memory settings;
invalid field values use defaults with a warning. Failed saves remain active in
memory and can be retried from preferences.
.PP
The default scrollback is 10,000 lines per tab. A limit of -1 means unlimited
and can consume more disk and memory. Search examines retained terminal output,
not shell command-history files. Profiles can be duplicated, renamed and reset.
Removing a profile moves affected tabs to the default profile.
.PP
The default terminal palette is dark. Window controls follow desktop appearance;
terminal profiles offer Dark, Light, System and Custom colors. Opacity affects
only the terminal background. Blur is a compositor feature.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
CLI-created sessions inherit the invoking process's environment, including when
forwarded to an existing instance. UI-created tabs inherit the application's
startup environment, not another shell's exports. TERM is set to xterm-256color,
COLORTERM to truecolor; inherited TMUX and TMUX_PANE markers are removed.
.PP
New UI tabs inherit the active tab's directory/profile. Local OSC 7 directories
are accepted; remote hosts are rejected. An account login shell is used unless
the profile names another executable.
.SH MOUSE
Selection and clipboard copy/paste are supported. Automatic copy-on-selection
is optional. VTE arbitrates application mouse reporting; hold Shift to use
terminal mouse selection or its context menu while an application captures the
mouse. PRIMARY/middle paste depends on compositor support.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a launch request was accepted, not that its child command succeeded.
Invalid arguments/profiles/directories return a nonzero status. Spawn errors are
shown in the tab. The application does not wait for the child when invoked as a
secondary client and does not return the child's exit status.
.SH NOTES
Closing a terminal normally hangs up its PTY. Close confirmation checks foreground
jobs and explicit commands, not every possible shell background job. Use tmux
when intentional session persistence is required. No image protocols are added;
Sixel is disabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR update-alternatives (1)
